Third-party data, models and code used by the scripts
----------------------------------------------------

Wikipedia
    The FRAMES-824 and MoNaCo-1315 corpora used in the paper are built from
    English Wikipedia articles (live revisions fetched in 2026). Wikipedia text
    is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
    International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0). Any redistribution of those corpora
    (including our published copies, roychowdhuryresearch/panini-dr-frames-corpus
    and roychowdhuryresearch/panini-dr-monaco-corpus) must credit Wikipedia
    contributors and carry the same licence.

FRAMES (google/frames-benchmark)
    Questions and answers are distributed by Google under the Apache License
    2.0 (see the dataset card). datasets/frames/prepare.py downloads them; they
    are not included here.

BrowseComp-Plus (Tevatron/browsecomp-plus, -corpus, -indexes)
    Queries and answers are distributed obfuscated, with a canary, so that the
    benchmark never appears as plain text online. We do not redistribute the
    queries, answers, corpus or indexes. The queries are decrypted with the
    authors' own script from a checkout of their repository. Never commit or
    publish the decrypted files.

MoNaCo (allenai/MoNaCo_Benchmark)
    Released under ODC-BY with the request "DO NOT redistribute the unzipped data
    files online" and a canary string. We do not redistribute MoNaCo questions,
    answers or gold annotations. datasets/monaco/prepare.py builds the question
    file locally from the official release. The MoNaCo corpus we publish
    (roychowdhuryresearch/panini-dr-monaco-corpus) is gated for the same reason:
    access requires accepting MoNaCo's terms.

openai/gpt-oss-120b
    Apache License 2.0. Served with vLLM (serve/gpt_oss_120b.sh); not bundled.

jinaai/jina-reranker-v3.5
    Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 (CC BY-NC 4.0). The paper
    configuration uses it as the reranker. NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY: commercial
    users must replace it (results will then differ from the paper). Not
    bundled; serve/jina_reranker.sh downloads it.

Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B
    Apache License 2.0. Query/document encoder for dense retrieval; not bundled.

BrowseComp-Plus grader template and MoNaCo V2 judge
    panini-dr score grades with the benchmark authors' own code: the
    BrowseComp-Plus grading template (texttron/BrowseComp-Plus, MIT) and the
    MoNaCo authors' V2 LLM judge (tomerwolgithub/monaco, which states no licence
    for its code). Neither is included in this repository.
    scripts/fetch_grader_sources.py clones both; src/panini_dr/eval/official.py
    loads them from the user's checkouts.

The panini-dr verify bundle
---------------------------

The bundle that panini-dr verify replays is published in the verify/
directory of roychowdhuryresearch/panini-dr-frames-corpus, not in this
repository. It holds recorded runs of the paper configuration on 8 FRAMES
questions and contains:

    - FRAMES questions and gold answers (google/frames-benchmark,
      Apache License 2.0);
    - passages of English Wikipedia text from the FRAMES corpus, inside the
      recorded prompts, reranker requests and traces (CC BY-SA 4.0: credit
      Wikipedia contributors and share alike);
    - recorded outputs of openai/gpt-oss-120b (an Apache-2.0 model), and the
      Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B query vectors and jinaai/jina-reranker-v3.5
      relevance scores that the recorded runs received.

It contains no BrowseComp-Plus or MoNaCo data.
